{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"cd67e9615e7d1d83f276826fc64bfaef25d965ef832c631567e24904f687b6a8","digest":{"component_or_area":"mcp service entrypoint and deployment","key_entities":["mcp-entrypoint.sh","tickets branch","autodeploy.sh","MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT","/health","Dockerfile.reviewbot","store_uninitialized","test_mcp_entrypoint_does_not_block_boot_on_the_tickets_clone"],"problem_keywords":["mcp entrypoint","synchronous clone","boot blocking","health gate","blue-green deploy","readiness timeout","rollback"],"propositions":["The mcp entrypoint synchronously clones the 199k-commit tickets branch before starting the server, causing the container to miss the 120s health gate deadline and triggering rollback on every deploy.","The service cannot answer /health within MCP_HEALTH_TIMEOUT while a blocking clone is in progress, so blue-green promotion fails and nginx upstream remains pointed at the stale old container.","The blocking-clone pattern copied from review-bot (a stop-and-start service) is incompatible with mcp's readiness gate requirement.","Tracker reads must degrade gracefully to store_uninitialized while the clone converges in the background, rather than returning empty results or blocking the container startup."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787904411103549001,"uuid":"0eead5c6-e7fb-4fda-8f17-134e0d1c1a37"}